    "rationale": "Final decision: keep the original artifact byte-for-byte (keep_bytes), no repair deployed, and submit its complete source with n_params = 5.\n\nEvidence: the only pre-registered probe was a symbolic term removal targeting param4 (the -d2*x**5 term). All three refit arms converged (original nmse 0.09180398722781567, canonical_full sham 0.09180398722781569, removed/4-param 0.09180470524756015). delta_nmse = 7.18e-07, far below epsilon = 1e-5, so the verdict is \"contradicted\" for the claim that removal costs more than epsilon; the sham drift 1.39e-17 is below tolerance 1e-10, which indicates the refit pipeline reproduces the parent numerically within the stated tolerance.\n\nWhy no edit: the single-term probe gives no support for a meaningful-gain edit (a train NMSE decrease > 1e-5 was never observed; the sham arm changes nothing and the removal arm changes NMSE upward in the 7th decimal). Per the decision contract, evidence against deleting a term does not license adding a new term or extra parameters, so I do not introduce e.g. an x**7 term or any extension. Evidence for simplification is also weak: although the 4-parameter arm's NMSE increase (7.18e-07) is below 1e-5 in this narrow train-split refit, a single-arm diagnostic cannot establish that the reduced form is a sound simplification for the executor's own fit, and the original commitments only asked about the bound probe. Keeping the unchanged artifact is explicitly legal, so I avoid an unverified structural change.\n\nUncertainty: (1) All numbers are researcher-seen development observations on oscillator1/train with fresh host scoring; they are not held-out results and support no physical-necessity, optimality, or generalization claim. (2) The probe covers exactly one term; it says nothing about whether the other four terms are individually necessary, and a broader removal sweep was not run. (3) checker_feedback is null, so no independent check result is available — the absence of a check is not evidence of success or failure. (4) The draft is never executed; nothing here is a statement about how this final artifact will score. (5) I cannot verify the exact original bytes beyond reproducing the supplied source string, so keep_bytes is asserted relative to the provided packet text.\n\nDeployment: raw_validation — I claim only that the final executor checks the raw submitted plan against its original syntax gate before any later token normalization; I do not claim the plan passes that gate. No repair was applied to any diagnostic copy, so probe_repair_deployed would be false.",
